{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/596304-fetish-questions-lore-of-the-forsaken-lodges-the-faithful-question","id":596304,"title":"Fetish questions ! \"Lore of the forsaken + Lodges the faithful question\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-19T17:20:19-07:00","id":596304,"title":"Fetish questions ! \"Lore of the forsaken + Lodges the faithful question\"","content":"In the book Lore of the Forsaken, around page 145 - 146, there is a section called &quot;Festish level evaluation system&quot;. It was designed in the time, to help guide any players, and the storyteller too, to be able to create, with some sort of balance, fetishes. <br /> <br /> The re is also a book called Lodges the faithful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have 4 question.<br /> <br /> 1- Is that book still a reference in the new God machine or if you prefer Idigam chronicle/werewolf the forsaken 2.0 ?<br /> <br /> 2- If the book is still a reference, would you consider the guideline there to create fetishes still adequate ?<br /> <br /> 3- Finally, is it too powerful in the Werewolf the forsaken 2.0 world, to have a powerful fetish weapon of rank 5, being able to deliver aggravated damage ? In werewolf the forsaken 1.0, it was possible according to those rules.<br /> <br /> 4- Is the book lodge the faithful still a reference, and do youthink that the lodge of arms still exist as it is written ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you very much for your answer !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T17:48:17-07:00","id":596348,"title":"","content":"Well, 2nd edition has its own guidelines for Fetish creation. I think a 5 dot Fetish weapon that did aggravated damage would be fairly reasonable, given how difficult it would be to craft. As for Lodges of the Faithful, we don't have any official mechanics for Lodges in 2nd edition, so for now it could still be used. However, Lodges will probably be updated eventually, either in a blog post or a supplement book, and they will probably work fairly differently than they did in 1st edition. Fluff wise, it's all still valid as far as I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T20:03:49-07:00","id":596425,"title":"","content":"Good. Thanks for the answer. Its because at some place in the book, it is written that a fetish rank 5 can simulate or act (don't remember the exact words) as a bane vs some types of creatures. Ex: Silver is the bane of werewolves. The thing is this: -Can it act as a bane vs everything ? Cause dealing aggravated to anyone, is sure looking like it. In the book lodge of the faithful, there is the lodge of arms. They do create a bound with a specific weapon, giving them +3 bonus dices to fight with it. Pretty powerful. Too powerful or just perfect ? Its because imagine a single werewolf player, being able to create like a fetish weapon rank 5... dealing aggravated damage, and then, bounding with it in the lodge of arms, getting an additional +3 dices to fight with that weapon. That would be quite powerful. Back in the time, it was possible according to the rules. It was like... putting all your eggs in the same basket, sure... but at the same time... it was like... &quot;omg&quot;. One of my player was getting there... and now, with the new God Machine rules and werewolf 2.0... he is wondering if everything he was trying so hard to do is still valid or completely overkill. I don't know what to tell him since Ido not have much experience in the nWoD 2.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T21:42:53-07:00","id":596490,"title":"","content":"A weapon that acts as a bane against everything and does aggravated damage against everything would certainly be considered overkill.<br /> <br /> Still, it might fit as a five dot fetish, with a Rank 5 spirit of violence or slaughter inside it. The way it works now is that the dot value of the fetish corresponds to the Rank of the spirit inside. Four dot fetishes can be, in terms of weapons, 'A weapon with a powerful enhancement such as increased damage,' but I think for aggravated damage against everything you'll need to go higher, five dot fetishes are considered, 'A truly deadly weapon like one that cuts Essence or Willpower as well as flesh,' and can also be, 'something that allows the Uratha to outright break some rules such as using their Defense against mental attacks or to count themselves as the bane of something that doesn't usually suffer a bane.'<br /> <br /> Reason suggests they're trying to limit it to one thing, like a bane to humans, and not everything in the World of Darkness, so you're pushing it, but it's your game to allow or forbid. At the point where you're doing aggravated damage like that, you wouldn't need to join the Lodge of Arms for a paltry +3 dice to combat rolls you could get elsewhere without making a potentially life-long commitment. Just max out your Weaponry and Strength, grab a specialization, and use an All Out Attack or Willpower for +3 a pop. Or both for +6. Odds are anything you hit with it isn't going to be standing around and fighting back anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2015, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T04:58:35-07:00","id":596720,"title":"","content":"I'm personally a bit leery with allowing the aggravated damage to everything bit. On the one hand, it takes a level 5 Rite with major drawbacks in order to deal aggravated against other wolves (which can be regenerated), and you need Rank plus certain Warding Gifts to qualify for dealing aggravated against most spirits, or going on quests to seek out a Bane for more powerful spirits. Aggravated damage is a handy thing in Werewolf because it does something additional to spirit prey that it doesn't do to anyone else - destroys essence. Aggravated damage can actually cause a spirit to flat out perish instead of just falling into slumber. <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, agg damage from only one source against a spirit and other lethal won't be enough to consume all the essence and you'll either need to drain the essence another way, or put the spirit to slumber - its almost all or nothing. The Hosts discorporate. Humans are already easy prey in combat, its getting them into claw range. Werewolves can just be fought using silver if you want agg damage. I don't think the Ridden are any different from regular humans when it comes to the difference between lethal and agg - there's the occasional Dread Power that has limited benefit, but most aren't an issue against a sacred hunt. <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't think it'll be too mechanically unbalancing to allow it from a combat standpoint. The problem that I can see, though? It would bypass plot. Spirit banes are designed to require quests to fulfill, which require hunts of a kind. Wolves have taboo about using either the ritual or silver against their own. Idigam are scary <i>things</i> that should be difficult to understand, and a desperate search for a way to kill; finding a fetish that acts as a bane would be an awesome story for a way to kill it. Generalized agg-dealing weapons have the potential to shift the tone of the game from a hunt, to just going out to slaughter enemies in combat machine mode. That would lead to an &quot;arms race&quot; between players and ST with their stats, and... well, I just think you need to consider if agg dealing fetishes are thematically appropriate for the setting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:10:33-07:00","id":596807,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain a sword of Spirit Slaying is the kind of artefact that would cause more trouble than it'd solve.<br /> <br /> Spirits would fear and hate whoever wielded it, and other werewolves would want it for it's power.<br /> <br /> Idigam are also weird and morphic enough that they aren't exactly spirits, so it wouldn't work for that either. Especially since they set out a strictly defined list of Banes, based on how they Coalesce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T08:50:52-07:00","id":597018,"title":"","content":"Wow guys, thanks.<br /> Everything did help me alot wrap my mind around this.<br /> <br /> Of course, it had me think.<br /> <br /> The weapon is of course a Katana. A popular choice, but also it does fit the theme cause the guy using it is a more than competent Ithaeur, that was practicing Iaido and Kenjutsu before his first change. The practice of those arts where not only a martial fighting side utility, but it also fits the focus, harmony and self control theme.<br /> <br /> I don't want him to become the enemy of the spirits and him being marked. He of course do not use that weapon that often to fght. When he does, its for the kill, nothing short.<br /> <br /> A good Katana, according to the history, was (within the design and limitations defined by a specific culture, natural ressources and etc) the most efficient small and nimble cutting blade. Some katanas where even tested on prisonners... and stories said that when a good katana was in the hands of a good wielder, he was often able to completly cleave in half, a human being from the right collarbone, to the left hip... cutting down diagonaly, through fleash and bones alike.<br /> <br /> When he first acquired the blade, its main purpose was to defeat enemies on the material side and not on the shadow world. He deal with spirits differently, and his blade is also used in some of his rituals, simply has a focus forse determination and concentration... A catholic priest will use a cross, he will use a katana. A native american shaman will use a feather and a sharp bone to write something on the ground, he will still use his katana.<br /> <br /> I could rule that the blade works (on aggravated) only on this side.<br /> Also, dealing aggravated damage to about just anyone is too much. I agree. I could rule that the blade could deliver aggravated damage, on a target, only AFTER having tasted his blood during the scene, and upon activation. Obviously, target without blood would be unnafected.<br /> <br /> Or... I would rule that the blade deal alot of damage, all lethal... but more than usual, but on any target. Simple has that. Any more idea that would fit the theme would be greatly appreciated !<br /> <br /> The primary use of the weapon is to kill material beings.<br /> The symbol of the weapon to him is control, harmony, balance, focus.<br /> <br /> What would be your rule and why ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:58:47-07:00","id":597045,"title":"","content":"I think the primary use of all weapons is to kill material beings. Is there any reason this one is special on it's own, or is it just special to him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2015, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:00:51-07:00","id":597073,"title":"","content":"Lol...<br /> Ok, weapon killing material being is quite the norm I agree. I was speaking of this cause on some previous post, someone was speaking about the fact that a weapon that could deliver aggravated damage to spirits might be potentialy breaking the rules, and also, drawing too much attention toward its wielder, but a bunch of angry nasty spirits. A weapon that only function in the material side of the shadow, and only on creatures with blood, could, in that sense, be more limitated, making it more balanced, despite his very powerful rank 5 damage potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:03:09-07:00","id":597075,"title":"","content":"If your goal is for this weapon is for it to be uniquely suited to one-shot kills, I'd just say the first attack in a scene after activating the Fetish counts as a Killing Blow and leave it at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:43:10-07:00","id":597108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The weapon is of course a Katana. </div> </div> </div> *falls into Kuruth* Did I mention that katana in RPGs is a death rage trigger for me? Okay, joking aside..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The primary use of the weapon is to kill material beings.<br /> The symbol of the weapon to him is control, harmony, balance, focus.<br /> <br /> What would be your rule and why ? </div> </div> </div> My rule? First, I would start with the legend of the Muranasa and Masamune. Two legendary blacksmiths, arguing over which was the better, challenged each other by placed their finest swords in a river. The Muramasa would cleanly slice through any fallen leaf or flower that touched its blade, destroying it. The Masamune, however, didn't slice a single leaf. Instead, the leaves sliced by the Masamune were restored, healed of the damage wrought by the Muramasa. For this reason, Muramasa, though a mighty weapon that could easily kill, was considered a cursed blade, for it could not discriminate between friend or foe. Meanwhile, the Masamune was considered the finer of the two, for it would not harm the innocent and undeserving.<br /> <br /> I feel like you're trying to turn something that's all about killing into something about clear headed harmony and balance. The two themes are kinda clashing, imho. If the weapon is used for killing, it will attract death, blood, and pain spirits to it, and the blade's spirits will encourage its user to use it more often, and feed the killing parts of it. How is the blade going to be used to promote that balance and harmony, when all the essence it produces is deathly?<br /> <br /> <br /> If all you want is a killing weapon, something that gives you Killing Blow (or, perhaps more interestingly, removes an opponent's Defense so you can use the K.B. merit) as Charlaquin suggested might be ideal. Truth be told, Killing Blow is currently the deadliest ability out of all the WoD lines at the moment. Alternatively, have it inflict some kind of tilt - nothing says killing blade like something that cripples you and leaves you defenseless. <br /> <br /> Truth be told, aggravated damage isn't that big of a deal in a fight. Its scary for those in Kuruth, because it means they're not healing every turn, but against mortals, Hosts, Ridden? Not that much different than pure lethal. In fact, additional lethal damage is generally a better option than dealing agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:31:48-07:00","id":597386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/596304-fetish-questions-lore-of-the-forsaken-lodges-the-faithful-question#post596304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3- Finally, is it too powerful in the Werewolf the forsaken 2.0 world, to have a powerful fetish weapon of rank 5, being able to deliver aggravated damage ? In werewolf the forsaken 1.0, it was possible according to those rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the new Fetish/Talen rules are my work. I wouldn't be keen on a 5-dot Fetish with that power, to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4- Is the book lodge the faithful still a reference, and do youthink that the lodge of arms still exist as it is written ? </div> </div> </div>Lodge of Arms probably still exists but looks somewhat different to its 1e incarnation. When the 2nd edition Lodge rules eventually have their reveal, it'll be clear why.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T00:51:15-07:00","id":598040,"title":"","content":"As has already been mentioned several times, one of the examples of the capacity for a 5 dot fetish is to &quot;to count themselves as the bane of something that doesn\u2019t usually suffer a bane.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now there's only one thing that could mean, which is that it does aggravated damage to something. Allowing it to do aggravated damage to everything would surely fit the idea of a legendary weapon fit for a hero, harnessing the power of a demigod bound in iron to fell his adversaries, but it does present an issue of breaking one of the main themes of the game by providing a one-button solution to every hunt. <br /> <br /> Still though, the example is there. It'd be silly to print that line and then tell people to avoid that logical conclusion entirely. I suggest putting a restriction or a hazard on it. Like it acts automatically as the bane of a certain kind of creature (Vampires, Earth Spirits, etc.), or it has to taste the blood/essence of something before it can act as its bane (thus retaining at least some of the aspects of the hunt), or every attack with it is a kuruth trigger.<br /> <br /> Personally as long as you're running the game strictly, make the pack hunt down an appropriate Dihir and run through the logical consequences of such an action as well as deal with the aftermath, I'd be fine with it. That's in the hands of the ST though, the pack should have to go through hell to get and keep it.<br /> <br /> Optimally I think such a weapon should be something that the pack is weary to take on the hunt. Something that is hidden beneath floorboards or in places that aren't for only the most dire of circumstances or dangerous of hunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T15:04:39-07:00","id":681429,"title":"","content":"-clears throat- not sure if it's been mentioned yet, or if it even helps the op, but one might look into cursed items. A katana used on prisoners might be cursed after an amount of death and bloodshed. Doesn't necessarily follow fetish rules, but it's more naturally occurring then a fetish that may require someone to have 5 dots in crafts and rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T20:17:26-07:00","id":681712,"title":"","content":"Let's take an iconic, rank 5 weapon which does aggravated damage from first edition: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#845A4A\"><span style=\"font-family:Treefrog\">SAMPLE GRAND KLAIVE \u2014 THE LABRYS (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">This mighty double-headed ax was created by a female Rahu of the Lodge of Garm. The Labrys howls when used to strike a male opponent, and no human man can lift the mighty fetish. (No mundane human male can budge the item, although human women and any supernatural beings can operate it normally, as can any werewolf in Hishu form.) It inflicts aggravated damage against males, regardless of their species. It functions normally against women of any species, inflicting lethal damage.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><b>Action: </b><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Reflexive</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T17:01:03-07:00","id":730404,"title":"","content":"Some Home-made fetishes following the guidelines on the corebook:<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022) Devil's Hand Glove<br /> Single leather glove that grants the Ambidexterity merit (pg. 164 GMc) when worn.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Thrashing Snake Belt<br /> Snake skin belt that grants the Double Jointed merit (pg. 165 GMc), and applies it's penalty even when performing aggressive actions.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Draught of the World-Tree<br /> The bitter spirits collected in these old moonshine bottles, decorated with First Tongue glyphs of understanding and memory etched in wax contain powerful spirits of knowledge bound within. Once the user drinks the contents of the bottle in their entirely (extended Stamina + Resolve rolls, need 5s, each roll takes 10 minutes), he gains either:<br /> <br /> * Influence (Knowledge) 3, <br /> * Access to a Knowledge gift facet as if it's relevant renown was 3 dots (This version costs 4 dots), <br /> * The Encyclopedic Knowledge merit tied to any skill and Eidetic Memory. <br /> <br /> These effects last for 24 hours and the bottle must be refilled with 30 years old Whiskey (Availability 2) before it can be used again, the alcohol must rest there undisturbed for a week.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022) The cat's blessed shoes<br /> These black Air Jordan One sneakers have a cat spirit bound within them, and their laces are feline tendons. The wearer has access to all five dots of the Parkour merit when worn &amp; activated. Activating them takes clicking their heels together.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) The Blood-Thorn's Knife.<br /> This knife with fresh, live vines tied to it's pommel allows it's user to summon terrible impaling vines from under their enemies when using the Black Earth, Red Hunger Glory Facet of the Nature's Gift. In order to activate the Fetish, the Uratha must stab his hand onto the earth (Thus taking 1L damage and it won't work on a concrete or asphalt settings, for example) with a successful Strength + Weaponry - Defense roll and someone he can see is subject to his successes on the roll as Lethal damage. Alternatively the user can stab the ground without bleeding himself, but then successes are applied on a ranged restrain action (See Grapple, WtF2e pg. 167), This attack is contested by the Strength + Brawl of the target and still penalized by his or her defense, if the target fails, he's considered held. The vines have a durability of 3 and size equal to the successes achieved on the activation. The User can also spend multiple essence (beyond any activation) in order to apply +1 to the damage of the attack, with each point spent adding to it in such a fashion as it makes the vines more gruesome, also adding to vine's durability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T20:10:16-07:00","id":730913,"title":"","content":"1st ed gave away agg damage like it was Christmas, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T00:00:51-08:00","id":770569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/596304-fetish-questions-lore-of-the-forsaken-lodges-the-faithful-question?p=730404#post730404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Home-made fetishes following the guidelines on the corebook:<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022) Devil's Hand Glove<br /> Single leather glove that grants the Ambidexterity merit (pg. 164 GMc) when worn.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Thrashing Snake Belt<br /> Snake skin belt that grants the Double Jointed merit (pg. 165 GMc), and applies it's penalty even when performing aggressive actions.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Draught of the World-Tree<br /> The bitter spirits collected in these old moonshine bottles, decorated with First Tongue glyphs of understanding and memory etched in wax contain powerful spirits of knowledge bound within. Once the user drinks the contents of the bottle in their entirely (extended Stamina + Resolve rolls, need 5s, each roll takes 10 minutes), he gains either:<br /> <br /> * Influence (Knowledge) 3,<br /> * Access to a Knowledge gift facet as if it's relevant renown was 3 dots (This version costs 4 dots),<br /> * The Encyclopedic Knowledge merit tied to any skill and Eidetic Memory.<br /> <br /> These effects last for 24 hours and the bottle must be refilled with 30 years old Whiskey (Availability 2) before it can be used again, the alcohol must rest there undisturbed for a week.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022) The cat's blessed shoes<br /> These black Air Jordan One sneakers have a cat spirit bound within them, and their laces are feline tendons. The wearer has access to all five dots of the Parkour merit when worn &amp; activated. Activating them takes clicking their heels together.<br /> <br /> Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) The Blood-Thorn's Knife.<br /> This knife with fresh, live vines tied to it's pommel allows it's user to summon terrible impaling vines from under their enemies when using the Black Earth, Red Hunger Glory Facet of the Nature's Gift. In order to activate the Fetish, the Uratha must stab his hand onto the earth (Thus taking 1L damage and it won't work on a concrete or asphalt settings, for example) with a successful Strength + Weaponry - Defense roll and someone he can see is subject to his successes on the roll as Lethal damage. Alternatively the user can stab the ground without bleeding himself, but then successes are applied on a ranged restrain action (See Grapple, WtF2e pg. 167), This attack is contested by the Strength + Brawl of the target and still penalized by his or her defense, if the target fails, he's considered held. The vines have a durability of 3 and size equal to the successes achieved on the activation. The User can also spend multiple essence (beyond any activation) in order to apply +1 to the damage of the attack, with each point spent adding to it in such a fashion as it makes the vines more gruesome, also adding to vine's durability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetish (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Maddening Visage<br /> The Glorious Lunacy facet of the Dominance Gift allows the user of this metallic choker, warm to the touch to inflict Lunacy even to the monstrous denizens of the world, not including the Awe-Struck condition. Uratha need to be suffering from the condition associated with a Hunter Aspect in order to gain a lunacy condition. Other facets that modify Lunacy work as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-21-2015, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}